# Requests to try the API from Visual Studio or VS Code (REST Client). Start the API first.
@api = http://localhost:5081

### One page of jobs
GET {{api}}/api/JobCatalog?page=1&pageSize=25
Accept: application/json

### One job in full (use an ID from the page above)
GET {{api}}/api/JobCatalog/4476446382
Accept: application/json

### Invalid page size (400)
GET {{api}}/api/JobCatalog?page=1&pageSize=0

### Unknown job (404)
GET {{api}}/api/JobCatalog/123

### Journal: the newest runs of both steps
GET {{api}}/api/Journal/runs?take=10
Accept: application/json

### Journal: a step 1 run (FetchJobListing) with all its entries (use a run id from the list above)
GET {{api}}/api/Journal/job-listing/runs/1?after=0
Accept: application/json

### Journal: a step 2 run (FetchJobDetails), only the entries after entry 10
GET {{api}}/api/Journal/job-details/runs/1?after=10
Accept: application/json

### Start an acquisition (202 Accepted; 409 Conflict if one is already running). Then follow it in the journal.
POST {{api}}/api/JobFetcher
Accept: application/json

### Stop the acquisition started by the API (202 Accepted; 409 Conflict if none is running here)
POST {{api}}/api/JobFetcher/stop
Accept: application/json

### The API description (Development only)
GET {{api}}/openapi/v1.json
